d75c4b51","cmd-14044722f9f14475","cmd-2d14c9ef429a4b4f","cmd-82403597ad484fb1","cmd-cfd5ea7bd3a0477f","cmd-3e1861307fb94857","cmd-83e42586abd14c33","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration and behavioral evidence. Node1 demonstrably served NTP to node2, while node2 used node1 as its sole configured and selected source. The provider-wide restart protocol was successfully completed on both nodes, including healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and observed interruption, changed boot identities, and recovered configuration, service, and synchronization state.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots inventory /tmp but not /etc, so continued existence of the rollback configuration copies is inferred from their successful creation and the absence of a removal command rather than independently inventoried.","The retained diagnostic files are small evidence artifacts; their contents and exact storage impact were not measured."]}
